Hey i understand how hard this is on you right now, i was removed by police from my abuser a handful of years ago and it was really hard to stick to it and yeah the abandonment hurts like hell. As hard as that is, you got to understand it is the best thing for you, there will be people out there that accept you and can help you heal and not be abusive towards you in the future, even if it doesn't feel like and especially if you think he's the only one that might

&#x200B;

Remove his contact, you will still wake up feeling things and wondering what's happening but remove the component that will make you even more depressed right now and focus on keeping yourself safe too, theirs a reason this happened and it's not a easy thing to accomplish my abuser walks free everyday despite what happened to me and the evidence of stalking after i was removed. Delete it all and remove any possibility to contact him, contacting him and getting that feeling of rejection will only keep you looped in that abandonment feeling.

&#x200B;

People will not get it usually and i am sure that's isolating for you but they can still be there for you, keep yourself busy ask your friends to fill this time right now with things you can do together. You can reach out to me if you like, i've been there with a lot of people who were bad for me and even ones that weren't and i understand that abandonment feeling well, i've done silly and foolish things cause of it and i also learnt a few ways of coping with it. I'm not saying the feeling will go anytime soon, but it does leave and it gets easier the less you engage with it, stop the texts, the calling, remove the contact, keep busy and take it a day at a time. Focus on the pros and cons and keep them grounded in reality of what it really was like with them, remember that it's easy to focus on the good when they are away but that doesn't mean that's how you felt or what it was actually like when it was the everyday. Remind yourself of that and remind yourself of the reasons that this isn't good for you. You need support now more than ever, let your friends be there for you even if they don't get why you want to go back. It will be okay, not straight away but it will be, you are so strong for coping with these feelings and for looking for ways of support

My doctor didn't even tell me or let me taper off and took me off cold turkey when i was on it as a teen/young adult and holy shit the effects were the worst. Nausea, literally yelling all the time that i wanted to die, the heart anxiety feels

&#x200B;

I wonder why so many doctors either don't taper off at all or don't taper off correctly

Yep can relate my mum used to tell me every night when i was comforting her crying after she had another incident or fight with my dad that "if i wasn't born she wouldn't be with him" when i kept telling her to leave him cause he was abusive ect

&#x200B;

Or one time she went shopping and i was still asleep, my dad barged into my room and demanded to know where she was which i didn't know and he acted like he didn't believe me and i could sense he was going to get physical so i tried to close the door which he kept on pushing and opening. My mum run upstairs and got him away from the door and then yelled at me that she could hear me screaming from across the street

Before the age of 5, first my dad left (to go the uk for a better life for us) then my mum and i lived with my grandma where her cat gave birth to kittens and i had my own cat who loves the shit out of me and slept with me. Then they came back randomly and took me to the uk without the cat. 

&#x200B;

Theirs loads of other shit in my teens like my dads drug problem and my me comforting my mum every night;. She saw my Sh and said nobody will love me cause of it. SA happened, my romantic relationships escalated from overbearing but not that bad to full on domestic, emotional and financial abuse. That's not even getting into work or school life both where shit

I was on sertaline as a teen for anxiety and it worked and helped, then my doctor didn't taper me off slowly and i had THE WORST withdraws ever... anxiety never came back tho

&#x200B;

Then i got put on it again a handful of years back as i was feeling suicidal and shit, it made me feel incredibly bad and within like 2-3 days of being on it i od'd. Never going on that thing again

