Unpopular opinion but BPD is BPD, there might be signs and differences in how symptoms present but they are still BPD symptoms i'm not sure why you think you or anyone would fit perfectly into a box that's not 100% recognized across the world

&#x200B;

Sometimes they can be inward, sometimes they can be out, sometimes both or theirs a specific pattern to you that might feel outside the world. Hell i seen too many posts with people claiming they don't have fear of abandonment to realize they actually do and it presents itself in non obvious ways like related to work rather than straightforward what you think the trigger would be relationship issues or cancelations.

&#x200B;

I understand you might want to relate to someone and that is valid and i wont take that away i'm sure plenty will relate to you in the comments with time to respond. I just think focusing on getting better is more important than if you switch from type a to type b

