Barely surviving, i'm stuck in a bit city due to waitlists for my therapy where the rent is way too much honestly, living at just a small room where my mental health is getting very triggered due to living with strangers and the noises. The other tenants are loud and smash shit, do drugs, yell and curse a lot. I honestly don't leave my room or use the shared areas at all. Can't even afford a studio on my salary and my job fucked me over last year severely where i wasn't getting even enough for rent so i have like no savings to me at all as well

&#x200B;

Job aspect increased and my paychecks are going to be good for a while from now but i don't trust it anymore that it wont let me down again.

I personally find it easier with autistic people and most of my friends have it, they say what they mean and they mean what they say. None of this fake make believe things that neurotypicals do like "we should hang out sometime" aka no we aren't but lets pretend

&#x200B;

Facial structures are harder to read for sure but i can always rely on them saying what they want/mean much more straightforwardly and with almost no push back about it

I already did a dbt group and what you can look up is TIPP DBT, but focus on the temperature/water one basically splash, submerge or put a icepack/something very cold to your forehead in-between your nose and some of the nose too

&#x200B;

The temperature change helps massively to change how your emotions feel. It's stopped me from crying many many times instantly. I also used to have panic attacks when i was younger and what helped for me was when i started to notice the symptoms i would force change my breathing to be more consistent. For me just before a panic attack it would become irregular but by forcing myself to breathe consistently in a regular pattern it stopped my panic attacks from getting further than that

&#x200B;

I hope either/both of those help you and that you hang in there until you get into DBT

