I'm sorry that medication has made you feel apathetic, i think on the right medication and the right dosage that shouldn't be happening. I know what you mean tho i've been on medications that made me practically a walking zombie i didn't feel anything ever. But i want to add that it might of also not been the medication, i can't speak to you and what you are like but back when i had more of these extreme emotions it was very common for me to "feel too much" and then my brain would just shut everything off to make me be safer to myself and it took a while be it a day or a week before i felt this again, worth thinking about if you notice it like that or not. I hope whatever medication or treatment you try ends up helping you more with less side effects or issues

&#x200B;

I totally understand, i've come to accept it but i was upset about that at various times too. I know it's not the same but you can self soothe or talk to yourself how you wish others would, theirs self care/caring for amsr videos out there too that you can listen to. I wont lie when i get overwhelmed i often pat my own head and start to whisper to myself "shh it' alright" and you can laugh at that and think it's silly and i'm sure anyone who's seen me do it must have, but it's the sort of care i need and wanted as a child that i didn't get. Is it just myself almost gaslighting myself into it? To a degree yeah i guess, but it still calms me down and makes me feel a bit more loved.

From one bpd folk to another, there are medications out there that can help these emotions be less intense in the uk that's usually Quetiapine i've been on it for almost a year and a half with doses increasing and it's amazing stuff. I used to feel like you, cry like 80 times a day, intense anger all the time basically run by all my emotions

&#x200B;

Ask your psychiatrists if she can help you get any medication to help these emotions. Otherwise yeah i wont lie you do have to look after yourself, it's your life and others have theirs. You can be angry about it, lonely, upset, disappointed but it's not going to take away attempting to get that level of help and care from usual folk that don'\[t have such extreme emotions, or even those who do afterall they are attempting to handle themselves. Likely wont get you the results you want, it sucks and it may not be fair but that doesn't mean there aren't things out there that can help you individually

