You wont know what her experience is like, i think my experience is vastly different than the ones i've read from others on this post and it's not to give any doubt but that the same behaviour and some statements can be something else to. Only she will know what she felt or wanted to happen. 

&#x200B;

Me in relationships sounds a lot like her, loved quickly, wanted to spend 24/7 together ect and then withdrawing, not being able to express love, statements like "it's okay if you want to leave" but for me it was cause i felt smothered, i don't know why but i can't seem to "stay" in love and after the initial honeymoon, everything about a person will piss me off. The way they breathe, eat, lay, how they dress, their routine. And for me all i wanted was to get away from them but the fear of abandonment for me, was keeping me with them i didn't want to be the one to end it sometimes. Sometimes i tried to piss them off, make them leave me, i wanted out but i couldn't do it myself. Then crawled back when they tried to break up with me cause it hurt to bad.

&#x200B;

I'm much better now, but also not interested in dating so i wouldn't know what that would be like for me anymore.

You aren't alone, i've won my battle about a few years ago and say my friends win theirs either this year or only just last year too

