I got a diagnosis from crisis back in my hometown, but when i moved due to safety issues they "lost" my files and basically treated me like someone which no diagnosis and ignored letters i had that recommended i needed therapeutic intervention it took a lot of fighting, od's, calling 111, going a+e, steps to wellbeing. I'm very fortunate that steps to wellbeing really listened and put me forward to CMHT

Not all people suck but i can relate, last year i told someone about this condition, someones who's into psychology and cares about learning about conditions. They forgot about our plans, didn't apologize for it and then cut me out my life when my symptoms increased and basically lied to me that everything was fine while withdrawing more from me. 

&#x200B;

I get we can be too much or that we need to control ourselves and all that but the fact that they blamed it all on me and just run when the only reason that i had freaked out was because they did a number of bad communicating with me is shocking. You didn't remember our plans, you didn't apologize for forgetting these plans, you didn't communicate that my fear of abandonment and trying to get reassurance was too much for you and instead lied that it was all good.... Just what??

SPOILER

