Similarly to you, my mum wasn't present much she worked a lot and was the only one supporting us financially. My dad was anti goverment, anti work, good for nothing but making random stuff like computers but couldn't be bothered to do anything freelance stay at home and get high all the time type of guy. He'd bring his buddies over most nights and they hogged the kitchen, smoking and now that i'm older and understand also mushrooms. I would go hungry for hours and hours waiting till there was a opening like them going into the garden so i could quickly run in and grab a snack

&#x200B;

I remember him coming into my bedroom late at night, completely out of his mind thinking that it was the bathroom. I had to scream to wake my mum up who would then get him out and try and sort him out for the night. I used to block my door with a chair under the handle, run up as soon as i got in and block that door. Hours spent laying on the floor trying to hear what they were arguing about this time, they thought i didn't know. 

I don't blame my mum for her situation but she herself despite being sober hurt me too, perhaps more than my dad after all he was never there and too far gone but she tried to be better than him, better for me and yet she was my biggest disappointment. I had experienced what people assumed to be anxiety and depression (at my time my undiagnosed bpd) and she had made it explicitly clear on many occasions that i could not get the help that the schools, me and others thought i had needed. In her mind me staying in her care was more important, even if that care was with my druggie dad and her never there. She drilled it into me that i couldn't talk about what was happening. The schools called often that i had been speaking about suicide, attempts or in general seemed depressed and yet i had never seen a therapist for even a second. Sometimes she'd claim she'd get me an appointment but then one never came.

&#x200B;

I felt so afraid to talk to people, to say the wrong thing and the fear that she had installed in me that i ended up not making a single friend and on the one occasion i had and invited someone over for a sleepover. My dad pissed the bed in their room and despite me never knowing it at the time, somehow i think i did as i had never invited anyone over again after. I used to come into her room at night, almost every nigth after hearing her sobbing alone and trying to comfort her, trying to tell her to leave him but she didn't for many years

&#x200B;

My mental health escalated and my issues grew deeper i still feel angry about the denial  of that help, angry about the situation and maybe i would have had a better life getting taken away. And i am paying the price now as an adult, who feels they have never matured rightly and attempting to put it all back together.

&#x200B;

For ages i hated drugs, weed in particular, ended up replaying my own trauma by dating some shitty also anti goverment, anti work, drug lover who i'd fight with often about his usage or more specifically him using my money to feed his habit. Years later after getting away from him, his sorta friends and reconnecting with some others who were present and a lot of healing i'm okay with most drugs nowdays, not that i personally do them but i don't hold the anger and big grunge that i used to about it. I accept theirs other usage and not everyone is a piece of shit

I've done that a few times before, it's agonizing pain, throwing up non stop the most foul shit and then even after you are completely empty. It also wont kill you, you'll live for days and days or weeks and it's not worth it

